WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.140 --> 00:02:00.000
[Music]

00:02:22.040 --> 00:02:26.650
In diagnosing gonorrhea, we are concerned
not only with the clinical and epidemiologic

00:02:26.650 --> 00:02:31.860
evidence but laboratory evidence as well.
All physicians however may not be equipped

00:02:31.860 --> 00:02:33.400
for laboratory diagnosis.

00:02:33.400 --> 00:02:38.760
In such circumstances it is wise to act on
a provisional diagnosis based on history and

00:02:38.760 --> 00:02:45.690
symptoms while waiting for laboratory confirmation.

00:02:45.690 --> 00:02:51.459
True diagnosis rests on finding the gonococcus
by study of cultures and smears or, to use

00:02:51.459 --> 00:02:56.290
the word that is gaining preference, spreads.
Since facilities for culture study are not

00:02:56.290 --> 00:03:02.760
available to all physicians, many must depend
upon the spread alone.

00:03:05.900 --> 00:03:12.060
In any case, our concern is to secure material
for laboratory study. The profuse discharge

00:03:12.150 --> 00:03:19.150
of acute gonorrhea makes this a simple routine
matter both in the male and in the female.

00:03:20.360 --> 00:03:25.460
However, a thick spread makes study difficult,
so special care should be taken to make the

00:03:25.470 --> 00:03:32.470
spread for gram-staining thin and uniform.
This is best accomplished by rolling the material

00:03:32.569 --> 00:03:39.569
in the manner shown here.

00:03:39.709 --> 00:03:44.470
The story is quite different in chronic gonorrhea
in both sexes when the perfuse discharge is

00:03:44.470 --> 00:03:51.129
not present. Then it is often extremely difficult
to secure material for study.

00:03:51.129 --> 00:03:57.560
Yet here, careful diagnosis is most important.
Chronic gonorrhea is a focus of infection

00:03:57.560 --> 00:04:01.879
and a constant source of new cases of gonorrhea.

00:04:01.879 --> 00:04:06.129
As diagnosticians, we must be familiar with
those structures where the gonococcus may

00:04:06.129 --> 00:04:11.640
be found and with the techniques for stripping
them.

00:04:11.640 --> 00:04:22.980
In the male, these structures that harbor
the gonococcus are the urethra, the prostate,

00:04:23.120 --> 00:04:30.120
Cowper's glands and the seminal vesicles.

00:04:31.120 --> 00:04:36.640
Stripping these structures will yield material
for study. Of course it is realized that procedures

00:04:36.650 --> 00:04:40.740
for stripping these structures are dangerous
in the presence of acute gonorrhea and that

00:04:40.740 --> 00:04:47.740
they belong only to the chronic stage of the
disease and among the tests for cure.

00:04:50.140 --> 00:04:57.400
Stripping the urethra is a simple and familiar procedure.

00:04:59.660 --> 00:05:06.660
The prostate, however, being highly susceptible to trauma, requires gentle and correct massage.

00:05:10.110 --> 00:05:16.250
The safest and least painful method is to
pass the finger well up over the lateral lobe,

00:05:16.250 --> 00:05:23.250
bringing it down in a direction parallel to
the midline.

00:05:32.660 --> 00:05:37.259
After both lobes are thus emptied, the finger
is pressed well up beyond the median sulcus

00:05:37.259 --> 00:05:43.080
of the prostate and brought several times
from there to the anterior extremity of the gland.

00:05:44.330 --> 00:05:50.600
In this form of massage, the dangers of complications
are reduced. The patient's comfort is perhaps

00:05:50.600 --> 00:05:54.650
the best guide as to the degree of pressure
to be used.

00:05:54.650 --> 00:06:00.030
Wisdom will always err on the side of gentleness.
Cowper's glands through manipulation, may

00:06:00.030 --> 00:06:02.520
also yield material for study.

00:06:03.260 --> 00:06:08.160
To find the gland, the tip of the finger is
drawn down over the arch of the pubic bone,

00:06:08.169 --> 00:06:11.400
about one-half inch to the side of the midline.

00:06:11.400 --> 00:06:16.419
As it drops from the edge of the bone it will,
particularly in thin patients, fall into a

00:06:16.419 --> 00:06:22.139
triangular depression. The gland is easily
felt by rolling the intervening tissues between

00:06:22.139 --> 00:06:26.900
the finger and the thumb. Gently rolling the
tissue will express secretor lurking in the glands.

00:06:33.310 --> 00:06:39.280
The seminal vesicles when stripped also provide
material for study. However since the prostatic

00:06:39.280 --> 00:06:44.360
secretion always contains pus when the seminal
vesicles are infected, it is rarely necessary

00:06:44.360 --> 00:06:46.120
to strip them.

00:06:46.120 --> 00:06:50.810
Stripping is resorted to when vesiculitis
is suspected, but the physician should wait

00:06:50.810 --> 00:06:56.229
until the acute stage of the disease has passed
and the chronic stage has been reached. 

00:06:56.229 --> 00:07:00.229
Only then can digital expression of the vesicles be done safely.

00:07:00.229 --> 00:07:06.680
To strip the vesicles, extend the finger beyond
the prostate and to the side of the midline

00:07:06.680 --> 00:07:13.680
and bring it downward and toward the midline
as shown here.

00:07:27.389 --> 00:07:32.349
With the use of these techniques, material
for spreads and cultures may be obtained from

00:07:32.349 --> 00:07:42.149
the urethra, the prostate, Cowper's glands
and the seminal vesicles.

00:07:45.240 --> 00:07:50.080
Secretions obtained by stripping any of these
glands are collected in sterile broth for

00:07:50.090 --> 00:07:57.090
cultural studies and stained for microscopic
examination.

00:08:09.110 --> 00:08:13.319
Of course, preparation of the material for
laboratory study presents no problem when

00:08:13.319 --> 00:08:20.319
the specimen is ample. However, stripping the urethra, the prostate and Cowper's glands

00:08:20.550 --> 00:08:25.639
may at times yield only a scanty discharge
and in such cases the following method may

00:08:25.639 --> 00:08:28.690
be used to prepare material for study.

00:08:28.690 --> 00:08:35.690
After stripping the various structures, secure
the first half ounce of urine voided.

00:08:58.000 --> 00:09:01.860
Then centrifuge the urine;

00:09:14.050 --> 00:09:18.140
And invert the tube, so that the urine flows
out leaving the sediment in the tip of the tube.

00:09:34.240 --> 00:09:40.060
Then place a very small amount of normal salt solution in the tube;

00:09:47.750 --> 00:09:52.830
And shake well so that the sediment is suspended
in it.

00:09:58.340 --> 00:10:03.160
Then centrifuge again.

00:10:12.760 --> 00:10:20.480
Invert the tube and obtain sediment from its
tip for examination.

00:10:39.510 --> 00:10:44.970
This material is subjected to spread examination
and where available, culture studies.

00:10:45.760 --> 00:10:48.660
So much for the male.

00:10:48.660 --> 00:10:55.660
Now to secure material for study in chronic
gonorrhea in the female.

00:10:56.520 --> 00:11:05.680
Material may be obtained from the urethra,
from the endocervical glands 

00:11:09.020 --> 00:11:17.880
and from Skene's and Bartholin's glands.

00:11:25.450 --> 00:11:30.550
To secure material for study from the urethra,
the urethral meatus is wiped with cotton to

00:11:30.550 --> 00:11:34.990
remove vulva secretions.

00:11:41.840 --> 00:11:48.440
The gloved finger is then inserted into the
vagina and the urethra is stripped from above downward, 

00:11:48.880 --> 00:11:52.580
the external meatus being pressed
rather firmly against the pubic bone.

00:11:53.140 --> 00:11:58.620
A small cotton wrapped applicator is inserted
about half an inch into the urethra.

00:11:58.700 --> 00:12:06.180
The applicator should secure enough material for stain and culture.

00:12:09.420 --> 00:12:14.839
Secretor from Skene's glands is expressed
by the procedure just described. No additional

00:12:14.839 --> 00:12:21.839
massage or manipulation is necessary. In obtaining
secretor from Bartholin's glands, first wipe

00:12:21.870 --> 00:12:27.019
the area of the duct with cotton.

00:12:27.019 --> 00:12:33.990
Then insert the index finger a short way into
the vagina and place the thumb on the outer

00:12:33.990 --> 00:12:40.810
side of the labia majora. The intervening
tissue is then gently squeezed.

00:12:40.810 --> 00:12:45.260
When secretion is obtained in this way, it
is usually too scanty to be secured on an

00:12:45.260 --> 00:12:50.760
applicator. The flat end of a toothpick or
a platinum loop is better suited for this purpose.

00:12:55.690 --> 00:13:00.160
In obtaining material from the cervix, it
is well to remember that in the chronic stage

00:13:00.160 --> 00:13:05.730
of the disease, the gonococci are deep in
the endocervical glands and usually not in

00:13:05.730 --> 00:13:10.410
the plug of mucus filling the canal. Thus
it is best to cleanse this canal with cotton

00:13:10.410 --> 00:13:15.490
held in a sponge forceps.

00:13:22.740 --> 00:13:30.100
Then make firm pressure on the cervix with
blades of a bivalve speculum;

00:13:39.160 --> 00:13:45.389
And obtain the material thus expressed for
study.

00:13:45.389 --> 00:13:52.139
If spreads of these secretions are thin and
uniform, examination will be facilitated.

00:13:52.139 --> 00:13:57.170
If we rely on the techniques described, we
will find that material for test and study

00:13:57.170 --> 00:13:58.769
is always available.

00:13:58.769 --> 00:14:02.829
All of these materials from the male and the
female can of course be used both for

00:14:02.940 --> 00:14:07.920
cultures and spreads.

00:14:13.520 --> 00:14:19.240
Mastery of these techniques will help provide
laboratory evidence for diagnosis,

00:14:19.240 --> 00:14:24.280
and what is equally important: laboratory confirmation of cure.

00:14:28.340 --> 00:14:32.900
But as the laboratory checks the clinical
symptoms and general treatment, so in the

00:14:32.910 --> 00:14:38.040
case of chronic gonorrhea in the female, the
clinical symptoms and case history must be

00:14:38.040 --> 00:14:40.699
used as a check on the laboratory.

00:14:40.699 --> 00:14:46.070
This is necessary because in chronic gonorrhea
in women, the gonococcus will sometimes escape

00:14:46.070 --> 00:14:50.010
detection by both the gram stain and the culture.

00:14:50.010 --> 00:14:54.740
Consequently when the history is suspicious
and symptoms persist, the laboratory must

00:14:54.740 --> 00:15:00.089
be challenged, perhaps repudiated.

00:15:00.089 --> 00:15:04.980
In the case of the female with chronic gonorrhea,
we must be guided by epidemiologic and clinical

00:15:04.980 --> 00:15:11.410
evidence as well as by laboratory evidence.
If symptoms and history point to the gonococcus,

00:15:11.410 --> 00:15:15.910
treatment is definitely in order.

00:15:21.460 --> 00:15:28.760
To withhold treatment is to risk new infections
and grave complications for the patient.

00:15:38.630 --> 00:15:43.600
In any case, the procedure of treating on
suspicion cannot be challenged. We all know

00:15:43.600 --> 00:15:47.790
patients who come for exam and they never
return. We know that often we have a positive

00:15:47.790 --> 00:15:54.560
diagnosis from the laboratory but no patient.

00:15:58.580 --> 00:16:03.780
To treat on suspicion, to warn at once that
an infectious disease may be present and

00:16:03.920 --> 00:16:09.640
to urge the patient to act accordingly, is to
move towards gonorrhea control.

00:16:20.480 --> 00:16:25.949
Certainly where infectious diseases are concerned,
every physician feels that his responsibility

00:16:25.949 --> 00:16:32.949
extends beyond his patient. It extends to
the people the patient may infect.

00:16:40.560 --> 00:16:45.120
Since diagnosis is an integral part of the
patient's first visit and this first encounter

00:16:45.260 --> 00:16:50.080
with the physician has a profound influence
on the patient's later behavior,

00:16:50.220 --> 00:16:55.200
it may be in order to discuss further at this point, the patient and his doctor.

00:16:55.300 --> 00:17:01.339
Effective venereal disease control and good
case holding rest on the doctor-patient relationship

00:17:01.339 --> 00:17:05.510
and require that the patient be considered
as a total medical problem.

00:17:05.510 --> 00:17:09.539
The patient must be given an understanding
of the nature of his problem and he must be

00:17:09.539 --> 00:17:14.620
given an objective, which will impel him to
continue treatment.

00:17:14.620 --> 00:17:19.660
The patient may have syphilis. There may be
other complications. Certainly in a patient

00:17:19.660 --> 00:17:23.890
with gonorrheal infection, syphilis must be
considered.

00:17:23.890 --> 00:17:29.970
Ideally, the history of gonorrhea case follows
these general lines. The patient usually comes

00:17:29.970 --> 00:17:36.970
to the doctor's office three to six days after exposure, when the symptoms appear.

00:17:38.140 --> 00:17:41.340
Following the examination, the doctor takes material for a spread.

00:17:45.080 --> 00:17:49.200
He also takes a blood test for syphilis as part of the physical examination.

00:17:50.060 --> 00:17:53.640
It is too early to check for a syphilitic
infection which may have been contracted when

00:17:53.650 --> 00:17:59.010
gonorrhea was contracted. But the doctor explains
that the danger of such an infection exists.

00:17:59.010 --> 00:18:03.640
If possible, the doctor then gets the name
of the contact and speaks of bringing her

00:18:03.640 --> 00:18:07.940
under treatment. He also explains the nature
of the disease to the patient,

00:18:08.040 --> 00:18:12.800
in language that the patient can understand.

00:18:18.669 --> 00:18:25.669
The patient returns in three days for a second examination and to learn the laboratory findings.

00:18:25.960 --> 00:18:30.100
Let us assume that the findings of the test
for syphilis are negative. 

00:18:30.620 --> 00:18:32.900
The smear, however, is positive.

00:18:32.900 --> 00:18:36.740
Since treatment began with the first visit,
the doctor now simply checks the progress of the disease.

00:18:44.620 --> 00:18:49.919
Seven days later, the symptoms of most patients will have vanished. But now enough time may

00:18:49.919 --> 00:18:55.100
have elapsed for penile lesions to appear
if the patient also contracted syphilis.

00:18:55.100 --> 00:19:01.080
The doctor looks for lesions and if he finds
them, does a darkfield test at once.

00:19:01.080 --> 00:19:04.440
Let us assume that no lesions are found at this time.

00:19:04.440 --> 00:19:09.620
The patient returns again in seven days for two  reasons; so that the doctor can check the

00:19:09.620 --> 00:19:16.340
gonorrhea cure and look for penile lesions
again.

00:19:16.340 --> 00:19:22.330
We assume that again, no lesions are found.
The patient returns and is reexamined for

00:19:22.330 --> 00:19:26.640
infectious lesions at weekly intervals for
three weeks.

00:19:26.640 --> 00:19:33.640
Thereafter, every two weeks for another six weeks. A second blood test is part of the final examination.

00:19:34.630 --> 00:19:39.240
We have thus completed a three-month period of observation. The course of action described

00:19:39.240 --> 00:19:42.820
here has given the patient the fullest possible
protection.

00:19:42.820 --> 00:19:47.100
His gonorrhea cure has been determined, the
physician has also determined whether or not

00:19:47.100 --> 00:19:51.340
there was a syphilitic infection. The results
are good case holding 

00:19:51.520 --> 00:19:54.679
and effective venereal disease control.

00:19:54.679 --> 00:19:59.620
These are objectives that must be attained.
We know only too well that they will never

00:19:59.620 --> 00:20:06.620
come to us from the laboratory but only from
an appreciation of human relationships.

00:20:11.169 --> 00:20:15.179
When we speak of chemotherapy, we speak of
the weapon with which a change in history

00:20:15.179 --> 00:20:20.739
has been wrought. We speak of a swift, sure
and inexpensive cure for gonorrhea.

00:20:20.900 --> 00:20:26.040
Chemotherapy in gonorrhea has made difficult
and painful local treatment unnecessary except

00:20:26.200 --> 00:20:30.100
in the small number of patients who do not
respond to such medication.

00:20:30.110 --> 00:20:36.309
It is a great boon to the private physician,
to clinics carrying heavy caseloads, often

00:20:36.309 --> 00:20:42.020
with extremely limited personnel and of course
it is a great boon to the patient.

00:20:42.840 --> 00:20:47.800
In discussing this new treatment, it may be
well to recall an era of the past in order

00:20:47.809 --> 00:20:50.409
to dispose of it permanently for the future.

00:20:50.520 --> 00:20:54.720
Sulfanilamide was the first sulfa drug used
in the treatment of gonorrhea. 

00:20:54.880 --> 00:21:00.820
Although toxic reactions were frequent and sometimes grave, it continued in use for a time because

00:21:00.880 --> 00:21:05.720
a better substitute was not yet found.

00:21:05.740 --> 00:21:11.440
Because to tens of thousands infected with
gonorrhea, it offered the promise of a swift cure,

00:21:11.440 --> 00:21:18.400
a swift return to the jobs from which
the disease had taken them. This early sulfanilamide

00:21:18.400 --> 00:21:22.680
compound held out a hope to gonorrhea sufferers.

00:21:31.280 --> 00:21:37.900
But sulfanilamide produced toxic reactions
in many patients and created numerous asymptomatic carriers.

00:21:39.360 --> 00:21:44.080
Laboratories focused their attention
on finding a safer and more effective chemotherapeutic agent.

00:21:45.600 --> 00:21:51.940
New sulfa drugs were produced rapidly. Drugs
superior to sulfanilamide. As these more effective

00:21:51.940 --> 00:21:57.419
drugs appeared, leading clinicians and the
United States Public Health Service abandoned sulfanilamide.

00:22:00.860 --> 00:22:06.260
But sulfanilamide had been widely publicized and so it gave way, but slowly,

00:22:06.280 --> 00:22:11.000
to the more effective, safer drugs.

00:22:11.980 --> 00:22:17.740
Doctors continued to prescribe it. Patients
continued to ask for it. But there is no place

00:22:17.740 --> 00:22:22.060
for sulfanilamide in the treatment of gonorrhea.

00:22:22.160 --> 00:22:26.880
Today, the drug of choice is sulfathiazole.

00:22:29.120 --> 00:22:36.400
But research and experience indicate that
it may be entirely supplanted by penicillin.

00:22:36.409 --> 00:22:39.760
The toxicity of penicillin is negligible.

00:22:42.220 --> 00:22:48.440
The toxicity of sulfathiazole is low and the
reactions are mild. Rarely does the patient

00:22:48.450 --> 00:22:52.419
find it impossible to consume enough of the
drug to bring about a cure.

00:22:52.419 --> 00:22:58.789
Even when low blood concentrations are maintained,
the relatively high cure rate is achieved.

00:22:58.789 --> 00:23:04.370
Of course, there are a few people who cannot
tolerate any of the sulfa drugs in any concentration

00:23:04.370 --> 00:23:06.950
and so all patients must be watched. 

00:23:06.980 --> 00:23:11.000
This is no drug to be sold over a counter withouta prescription.

00:23:12.540 --> 00:23:16.100
Twenty grams is the recommended dosage for
a single course of treatment;

00:23:16.260 --> 00:23:20.660
four grams a day for five days.

00:23:23.760 --> 00:23:29.680
However, if this first course of sulfathiazole
fails to bring about a cure, medication should

00:23:29.740 --> 00:23:33.960
be discontinued for seven to ten days 

00:23:34.080 --> 00:23:37.900
and then a second course of treatment given.

00:23:40.860 --> 00:23:47.100
A number of patients will not be cured. Penicillin
should be considered. Penicillin therapy of

00:23:47.100 --> 00:23:51.220
gonorrhea may mock or delay symptoms of syphilis.

00:23:51.320 --> 00:23:54.700
Patient observation should be continued over three months.

00:23:54.710 --> 00:23:59.490
A special precaution against transmitting
a possible chronic infection, the physician

00:23:59.490 --> 00:24:05.559
should insist that a condom be used at every
sexual contact for three months after disappearance

00:24:05.559 --> 00:24:07.119
of symptoms.

00:24:08.000 --> 00:24:14.580
With the aid of these drugs, we can in a short
time make gonorrhea a comparatively rare disease.

00:24:32.400 --> 00:24:36.400
Prophylaxis is the other
great ally of gonorrhea control.

00:24:36.560 --> 00:24:42.480
Civilian and military health authorities now recognize its value and urge its widespread use.

00:24:43.320 --> 00:24:48.780
To make descriptions of approved techniques
available to physicians, these publications

00:24:48.789 --> 00:24:55.070
have been prepared and are furnished on request.
The greatest safety and preventive measures

00:24:55.070 --> 00:24:57.910
other than continence, belongs to the condom.

00:24:58.160 --> 00:25:01.900
But improper use of the condom destroys its value.

00:25:07.220 --> 00:25:12.580
Instruction of the patient is part of the
physician's role in implementing prophylaxis.

00:25:12.590 --> 00:25:17.419
Common habits such as using a condom only
at the end of intercourse should be condemned.

00:25:17.419 --> 00:25:22.929
The patient should also be warned to put on
the condom before his hand comes into contact

00:25:22.929 --> 00:25:28.789
with the woman's genitalia, lest he carry
the infection to his own organs before intercourse is begun

00:25:28.970 --> 00:25:34.480
These and other points need to be impressed
on the patient. The pamphlet shown is intended

00:25:34.480 --> 00:25:41.279
for lay education and can also be secured
from the United States Public Health Service.

00:25:41.279 --> 00:25:45.960
The prophylactic packet is sometimes effective
but here again, the patient needs instruction

00:25:45.960 --> 00:25:50.480
as to its proper use. Chemical prophylaxis
is most effective when administered under

00:25:50.480 --> 00:25:58.300
medical supervision. When administered soon after exposure, it is at least 90 percent effective.

00:25:58.680 --> 00:26:01.620
Prophylactic measures are not as easily applied
in women.

00:26:01.940 --> 00:26:05.360
Nor are they considered to be as efficacious. 

00:26:05.560 --> 00:26:13.040
There is no doubt that widespread use of prophylaxis will aid materially in controlling gonorrhea.

00:26:15.820 --> 00:26:21.580
Education of the public so that people will
not go to the quack but to the licensed physician;

00:26:23.260 --> 00:26:30.260
early diagnosis by the physician; correct
use of prophylaxis.

00:26:30.960 --> 00:26:41.160
 Sulfathiazole, penicillin:  these things are weapons in the hands of the medical profession.

00:26:42.730 --> 00:26:49.730
And most important in gonorrhea therapy, let
us remember this; a laboratory is not infallible.

00:26:51.880 --> 00:26:57.340
Clinical and epidemiologic findings are ample
grounds for treatment.

00:26:57.340 --> 00:27:02.990
If we use them as a basis for treatment, we
will eradicate many infections

00:27:02.990 --> 00:27:05.950
that in the past filtered through the diagnostic net.

00:27:05.950 --> 00:27:11.809
Certainly sulfathiazole and penicillin are
a promise and a challenge to the medical profession;

00:27:11.809 --> 00:27:17.350
an opportunity to wipe out one of our oldest
diseases, and an opportunity to save millions

00:27:17.350 --> 00:27:21.220
of man days lost to industry and the armed
forces.

00:27:21.220 --> 00:27:25.240
To prevent a great loss to the nation's health
and strength.

00:27:25.360 --> 00:27:41.060
[ Music ]

